      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1140964
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T09:01:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: This shifts the table entries down to the output bit depth *before* interpolation. In the C implementation (`SharpYuvLinearToGamma` in `sharpyuv_gamma.c`), the interpolation is performed at full precision (16.16) and only the final result is shifted down.\n\nShifting before interpolation loses precision and will likely cause this code to not be bit-exact with the C implementation, especially for lower bit depths or in steep parts of the gamma curve. You should perform the interpolation first and then shift the result.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 405,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "ade403154fbc49592f608d740495772128ef5ab3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
